---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

// Get current language from URL
const pathname = Astro.url.pathname;
const lang = pathname.startsWith("/id/") ? "id" : "en";

// Bump when the content below actually changes. Using new Date() here claimed
// the page was updated today, every day.
const CONTENT_UPDATED = new Date("2026-10-21");

const lastModified = CONTENT_UPDATED.toLocaleDateString(
  lang === "en" ? "en-US" : "id-ID",
  {
    year: "numeric",
    month: "long",
    day: "numeric",
  },
);

const meta = {
  title: "About Me",
  description:
    "Learn more about Rio Bahtiar \u2014 full stack software engineer building web applications, modernizing existing systems and integrating services.",
  image: "/smc.jpg",
};
---

<Layout
  title={meta.title}
  description={meta.description}
  image={meta.image}
  showTopBanner={false}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-8 sm:px-6 md:py-12 lg:px-8 lg:py-16">
    <article class="prose prose-lg md:prose-xl mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <!-- Cover Image -->
      <div class="not-prose bg-base-200 relative mb-8 aspect-[16/9] w-full overflow-hidden rounded-lg sm:aspect-[21/9]">
        <img
          src="/smc.jpg"
          alt="Cover Image"
          width={1200}
          height={630}
          loading="eager"
          class="h-full w-full object-cover"
        />
      </div>

      <!-- Article Header -->
      <header class="mb-12 text-center">
        <h1 class="mb-4 text-4xl font-bold md:text-5xl">{meta.title}</h1>
        <p class="mb-4 text-lg opacity-90 md:text-xl">{meta.description}</p>
        <div class="text-sm opacity-70">Last updated on {lastModified}</div>
      </header>

      <!-- Article Content -->
      <div class="space-y-6">
        <h2>Introduction</h2>
        <p>
          Hello! I'm Rio Bahtiar, a full stack software engineer based in
          Yogyakarta, Indonesia. I build and maintain web applications,
          modernize existing systems, and integrate services, with experience at
          Sekolah.mu and Tokopedia alongside independent client work. In my free
          time, I enjoy reading technical literature, staying active with
          swimming, and exploring the possibilities of technology through
          science fiction.
        </p>

        <h2>Education & Background</h2>
        <p>
          I hold a Bachelor of Computer Science (S.Kom.) in Information Systems
          from Universitas AMIKOM Yogyakarta (2010-2014). My academic
          foundation, combined with continuous self-learning and professional
          development, has kept me close to modern software development
          practices and emerging technologies.
        </p>

        <h2>Professional Experience</h2>
        <h3>Sekolah.mu (2022-Present) - Senior Web Engineer</h3>
        <p>
          Leading web product development across the Sekolah.mu learning and
          career ecosystem:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Developing web applications with Vue.js and Nuxt.js</li>
          <li>
            Supporting products including Sekolah.mu, Karier.mu, Talentics.id
            and Rencanamu.id
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Independent Software Engineer, Upwork (2019-2022)</h3>
        <p>Independent web development and ongoing client collaborations:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Lifepal:</strong> frontend and backend work on the WordPress
            site, decoupling it through the WP JSON API and migrating the
            frontend to Next.js, then converting it into a Multisite network for
            Lifepal's microsites
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Aisconverse:</strong> early development of Treweler, a
            commercial WordPress mapping plugin built on Mapbox GL JS, including
            its admin settings interface
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Lingble:</strong> building and maintaining WordPress
            microsites, Ghost sites, and Klipfolio dashboards for data and
            metrics
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h3>
          Tokopedia (2016-2019) - Software Engineer → Senior Software Engineer
        </h3>
        <p>
          Developed web products and distributed services, progressing to lead
          the Microsites team and manage WordPress infrastructure. Selected
          projects:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Promo Code Engine:</strong> distributed backend work with
            Golang, gRPC, Redis and PostgreSQL (2018-2019)
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Tokopoints Desktop:</strong> migrating the desktop
            application from Perl to React (2018)
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>WordPress to Go microservices:</strong> rewriting several
            WordPress services as Golang microservices
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Careers page:</strong> moving from Workable to Workday
            through Workday's SOAP API
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Help Center:</strong> migrating from Zendesk to Salesforce
            Knowledge through its API
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h3>SoftwareSeni (2015-2016) - Frontend & WordPress Developer</h3>
        <p>
          Built frontend interfaces and WordPress solutions for client projects:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>WordPress Developer (2016):</strong> themes, plugins,
            WooCommerce features and payment integrations
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Front End Developer (2015-2016):</strong> HTML, CSS and
            JavaScript interfaces built with design and product teams
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Earlier Experience</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Front End Web Developer, Local Tobacco (2015)</li>
          <li>Web Designer, Mata Terbuka Digital Agency (2014-2015)</li>
          <li>
            SEO Specialist, Muhammadiyah University of Yogyakarta (2013-2014)
          </li>
          <li>
            Computer Laboratory Assistant, STMIK AMIKOM Yogyakarta (2011-2012)
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Technical Expertise</h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
          <div>
            <h3 class="mb-2 text-lg font-semibold">Frontend</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>TypeScript & JavaScript</li>
              <li>Vue.js, Nuxt 4 & Nuxt UI</li>
              <li>React & Next.js</li>
              <li>Tailwind CSS</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="mb-2 text-lg font-semibold">Backend</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Bun, Elysia, Hono & Better Auth</li>
              <li>Golang, Node.js & Express.js</li>
              <li>PHP / Laravel & WordPress</li>
              <li>REST, GraphQL, gRPC & SOAP</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="mb-2 text-lg font-semibold">Data & Background Jobs</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>PostgreSQL, MySQL & Drizzle</li>
              <li>Redis & BullMQ</li>
              <li>Typesense</li>
              <li>BigQuery & MongoDB</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="mb-2 text-lg font-semibold">
              Infrastructure & Observability
            </h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Docker & Kubernetes</li>
              <li>DigitalOcean & AWS / S3</li>
              <li>Cloudflare WAF</li>
              <li>Grafana & Sentry</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="mb-2 text-lg font-semibold">Development & Delivery</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Bun workspaces & Turborepo</li>
              <li>GitHub Actions & CI/CD</li>
              <li>Vitest</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="mb-2 text-lg font-semibold">AI-Assisted Development</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Claude Code & Codex</li>
              <li>MCP integration</li>
              <li>Adversarial code review</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h2>Professional Philosophy</h2>
        <p>
          My approach to software engineering is built on three core principles:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Quality First:</strong> Writing clean, maintainable, and
            well-tested code that stands the test of time.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>User-Centric Design:</strong> Creating intuitive experiences
            that solve real problems and deliver genuine value.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Continuous Growth:</strong> Staying current with technology
            trends while sharing knowledge with the community.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          I'm passionate about building scalable solutions that make a positive
          impact, whether it's improving user experiences, optimizing system
          performance, or mentoring the next generation of developers.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</Layout>
